From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:28:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Shaders: the build script reads its folder at run time and
 stops when it finds no source

The script made the translator's fingerprint from `env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")`,
which is fixed when the script itself is compiled. Cargo does not compile a
build script again because its tree moved, so after a move the script read
a folder that was gone, found no file, and every build got the hash of
nothing (cbf29ce48422232584222325cbf29ce4, the hash's start value) and an
empty list of switches. The shader cache keys on both: cached shaders kept
the translations of older code, and switches that change a translation did
not reach them (fifteen builds on 2026-11-27 and 28).

Now the folder is the one cargo names for this run of the script, and a
script that finds no source file stops the build. The fingerprint of an
unmoved tree is what it was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/victory-shader/build.rs | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/victory-shader/build.rs b/crates/victory-shader/build.rs
index b10212507..42de96209 100644
--- a/crates/victory-shader/build.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-shader/build.rs
@@ -32,12 +32,27 @@ fn fnv(state: &mut [u64; 2], bytes: &[u8]) {
 }
 
 fn main() {
-    let src = Path::new(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")).join("src");
+    // The crate's folder as cargo names it for THIS run of the script, not
+    // `env!`, which fixes it when the script is compiled: cargo does not
+    // compile a build script again because its tree moved. After such a
+    // move (2026-11-27) the script read a folder that was gone, found no
+    // file and gave every build the hash of nothing and no switches: the
+    // cache key stopped following the translator, and cached shaders kept
+    // the translations of older code for fifteen builds.
+    let manifest = std::env::var_os("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR").expect("cargo sets CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR for a build script");
+    let src = Path::new(&manifest).join("src");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=src");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=Cargo.toml");
     let mut list = Vec::new();
     files(&src, &mut list);
     list.sort();
+    // No source, no fingerprint: stop the build rather than hand out one
+    // that every other build shares.
+    assert!(
+        !list.is_empty(),
+        "victory-shader's build script found no source file under {}: the translator's fingerprint would be the same for every build",
+        src.display()
+    );
     let mut state = [0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325u64, 0x8422_2325_cbf2_9ce4u64];
     let mut switches = std::collections::BTreeSet::new();
     for p in &list {
